Hi,

I've uploaded the results of a bulk rebuild for NetBSD/alpha
4.0 to

   ftp://ftp.NetBSD.org/pub/pkgsrc/packages/NetBSD/alpha/4.0_2008Q2/

A total of 2.8GB of packages were uploaded, for a total of 1626
packages.  The list of new packages or packages available in new
versions is:

R-2.7.0nb1, WordNet-3.0nb1, balsa-2.3.10nb14, bitlbee-1.2.2,
clamav-0.94, geeklog-1.4.1nb3, libxml2-2.7.1, links-2.1.0.36nb1,
links-gui-2.1.0.36nb1, mtree-20070710, p5-XML-Xerces-2.7.0.0,
postfix-2.5.5, postfix-2.6.20080903, python25-2.5.2nb3, rrdtool-1.3.2,
rt-3.6.7, rt-mysql-2.0.15nb6, rt-pgsql-2.0.15nb6,
ruby18-base-1.8.7.72nb1, tiff-3.8.2nb4, tk-8.4.18nb1,
tremor-tools-1.0.0.8nb9, vim-7.2.10, vim-gtk-7.2.10, vim-gtk2-7.2.10,
vim-lang-7.2.10, vim-motif-7.2.10, vim-share-7.2.10, vim-xaw-7.2.10,
wireshark-1.0.3, yelp-2.22.1nb1, and zoom-1.0.3nb3.

The source tree this was built from was updated 20 Sep 2008, and
the packages were built on a system running 4.0.

This will be the last update for this branch/os/version; the next
update will be based on the pkgsrc 2008Q3 branch.

Regards,

- H=E5vard


